248:     /// }
249:     /// ```
250:     ///
251:     /// # Errors
252:     ///
253:     /// This function will return an error if the supplied bytes contain an
254:     /// internal 0 byte. The [`NulError`] returned will contain the bytes as well as
255:     /// the position of the nul byte.
